{"dir":"out","method":"onMessage","args":[[{"type":"text","text":"Found it. Two things together freeze the capsule:\n\n- `useQuota` stops polling once every window reads **100%** (`refetchInterval` returns `false`)\n- `snapshot()` returns the last `rate_limits` event as-is, and Codex only sends one while a turn runs\n\n| Window | Capsule shows | After reset |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 5-hour | 100% | 0% |\n| Weekly | 100% | 12% |\n\nTreat a window as reset once `resets_at` has passed:\n\n```ts\nconst used = window.resets_at <= now ? 0 : window.used_percent;\n```\n\nThe reset rules are in the [Codex docs](https://developers.openai.com/codex/rate-limits); the dev server is on http://localhost:5173, and the code is in [src/quota/codex.ts](src/quota/codex.ts)."}],{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","usage":{"input_tokens":10,"output_tokens":8}}],"delayMs":180}
